Feature: ShoppingCart

  Demonstrates how the values of an Examples table reach every kind of step
  parameter of a Scenario Outline: a quoted value, a doc string and a data
  table. The doc string carries a content type, so the IDE highlights and
  formats it as JSON while SpecBinder still passes it as a plain String.

  Scenario Outline: Order a single product
    Given I have an empty shopping cart
    When I add "<product>" to the cart
    And I submit the order with the following payload:
      """json
      {
        "product": "<product>",
        "quantity": "<qty>",
        "total": "<total>"
      }
      """
    Then the order should contain the following lines:
      | product   | quantity | line total |
      | <product> | <qty>    | <total>    |

    Examples: Single-product orders
      | product        | qty | total |
      | Wireless Mouse | 1   | 29.99 |
      | USB-C Cable    | 3   | 26.97 |
      | Laptop Stand   | 2   | 70.00 |

  Scenario Outline: Apply a promotion to the order
    Given I have an empty shopping cart
    When I add "<product>" to the cart
    Then the order should show the following promotion details:
      | field     | value      |
      | promotion | <promo>    |
      | channel   | web        |
      | discount  | <discount> |

    Examples: Promotions
      | product        | promo    | discount |
      | Wireless Mouse | SPRING10 | 10%      |
      | Laptop Stand   | BUNDLE20 | 20%      |

  Scenario Outline: Build an order reference from fixed text and Examples values
    Given I have an empty shopping cart
    When I add "<product>" to the cart
    And I place the order with reference "ORD-<year>-<region>"
    Then the tracking link should be "https://shop.example.com/orders/<region>/<year>"

    Examples: Order references
      | product        | year | region |
      | Wireless Mouse | 2026 | EU     |
      | Laptop Stand   | 2026 | US     |
